    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d435-a1">

                <pb facs="0664" n="564" sameAs="frus:frus1884/pg564"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 388.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Assim Pasha to Mr.
                            Wallace.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Sublime Porte</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1884-04-30"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 30,
                        1884</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Monsieur l’Envoyé</hi>: The imperial ministry has had
                    the honor to receive the note your excellency was good enough to address it the
                    27th of last February (No. 204), relative to the affair of Dr. Pflaum.</p>
                <p>This communication presents no new considerations in the discussion which would
                    justify a modification of the views exposed by my Department in its verbal note
                    No. 73708, 6.</p>
                <p>Your excellency will permit me, therefore, to wait for the result of the measures
                    we have taken in relation to this affair with the ministry of justice and of the
                    interior.</p>
                <p>Accept, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>M. ASSIM.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
